  FINDINGS:
   · PROVISIONAL MONEY: 10.7% of the pilot team’s GWP (R7120 of R66520) is dialler-priced at a flat R89, not read from the money source, because the Power BI file stops 4 dialling days short of the dialler.
   · TL LOGIN CLASSIFICATION: a leader dialling under a code-shaped login (CB902TL) reads as "missing from the Agent List" until S.tlCbs arrives from /api/roster — 50 minutes shown as a roster defect that is not one.
   · SHIFT DENOMINATOR: 2 day(s) (2026-09-11, 2026-09-12) sit in the HR register but in no fact row, because the model’s calendar is built from sales/calls/tracker only. Employed Shifts — and every target multiplied out of it — therefore grows as the dialler catches up.
   · QA IDENTITY: the QA ingest is the only join in the system that does not go through resolveKey. It builds the code from the digits of "Sales Agent CB" alone — so CB-095 is stored as CB095 and never meets the Agent List’s CB95. The agent’s own card read "QA — not measured" for the whole pilot; correcting the spelling of the code alone moved the composite 11.2 points (Needs support → Needs support) and the framework scored from 70% to 90%.
   · NEW-CAMPAIGN TARGET: "Download & Test" is reported (correctly) but has no row in MTD_RULES.salesTargetMatrix and no Target cell on the Agent List, so its sales target is 0 and every %-to-target on that team section is blank — 68 sales measured against nothing.
   · TL HEADCOUNT: over a window that spans a movement, headcount is "agents who worked for me at any point" (10 rows for 9 people), not "my team today". The sales split is correct; the head count is a different question and the team-leader view should say which one it is answering.

